)F FUNCTION -                                                           00050020
  THE PROFILE COMMAND IS USED EITHER TO SPECIFY TO THE SYSTEM CERTAIN   00100001
  USER CHARACTERISTICS WHICH ARE TO BE USED TO CONTROL THE FLOW OF      00150020
  INFORMATION TO AND FROM THE TERMINAL OR TO LIST THE USER PROFILE.     00160001
  THE USER PROFILE IS RETAINED THROUGHOUT EACH TERMINAL SESSION         00170001
  UNLESS THE USER WISHES TO CHANGE IT BY ISSUING THE PROFILE COMMAND    00200001
  AGAIN AND SPECIFYING THE APPROPRIATE OPERANDS.                        00250001
)X SYNTAX  -                                                            00350020
         PROFILE   LINE('CHARACTER')/LINE(ATTN)/LINE(CTLX)/NOLINE       00360020
                   CHAR('CHARACTER')/CHAR(BS)/NOCHAR                    00370020
                   PROMPT/NOPROMPT  INTERCOM/NOINTERCOM                 00380020
                   PAUSE/NOPAUSE  MSGID/NOMSGID                         00390002
                   MODE/NOMODE  WTPMSG/NOWTPMSG                         00393002
                   PREFIX('PREFIX')/NOPREFIX    LIST                    00396002
  REQUIRED - NONE                                                       00400020
  DEFAULTS - FOR PREFIX THE DEFAULT IS THE LOGON USERID                 00450002
  ALIAS    - PROF                                                       00500020
  NOTE     - IF THE COMMAND IS ENTERED WITH NO OPERANDS, THE COMMAND    00550020
             IS IGNORED.                                                00600020
)O OPERANDS-                                                            00650020
))LINE('CHARACTER')                                                     00700020
           - SPECIFIES THE CHARACTER WHICH IS TO BE USED FOR            00750020
             DELETING A LINE.                                           00800020
    'CHARACTER'                                                         00810020
           - IS ANY VALID CHARACTER.                                    00820020
))LINE(ATTN)                                                            00830020
           - SPECIFIES THAT ATTENTION IS TO BE USED TO DELETE A LINE.   00840020
             THIS IS THE SYSTEM DEFAULT DELETE CHARACTER FOR THE        00840420
             KEYBOARD TYPE TERMINAL.                                    00840820
))LINE(CTLX)                                                            00842020
           - SPECIFIES THAT CTLX IS TO BE USED TO DELETE A LINE         00844001
             FOR THE TELETYPE TERMINAL. THIS IS THE SYSTEM DEFAULT      00846020
             DELETE CHARACTER FOR THE TELETYPE TERMINAL.                00848020
))NOLINE   - SPECIFIES THAT THERE IS TO BE NO LINE DELETING CHARACTER.  00850020
))CHAR('CHARACTER')                                                     00900020
           - SPECIFIES THE CHARACTER TO BE USED TO DELETE A CHARACTER.  00950020
    'CHARACTER'                                                         01000020
           - IS ANY VALID CHARACTER.                                    01050020
))CHAR(BS) - SPECIFIES THAT BACKSPACE IS TO BE USED TO DELETE A         01100020
             CHARACTER. THIS IS THE SYSTEM DEFAULT VALUE.               01150020
))NOCHAR   - SPECIFIES THAT THERE IS NO CHARACTER DELETE CHARACTER.     01200020
))PROMPT   - SPECIFIES THAT THE USER IS TO BE PROMPTED FOR NECESSARY    01250020
             INFORMATION.                                               01300020
))NOPROMPT - SPECIFIES THAT THE USER IS NOT TO BE PROMPTED FOR          01350020
             INFORMATION.                                               01450020
))INTERCOM - SPECIFIES THAT THE USER WILL ACCEPT MESSAGES FROM OTHER    01500020
             TERMINAL USERS.                                            01550020
))NOINTERCOM                                                            01600020
           - SPECIFIES THAT THE USER WILL NOT ACCEPT MESSAGES FROM      01650020
             OTHER TERMINAL USERS.                                      01700020
))PAUSE    - SPECIFIES THAT SECOND LEVEL MESSAGES WILL BE AVAILABLE     01860020
             TO THE USER WHILE OPERATING IN A COMMAND PROCEDURE.        01870020
             IF SPECIFIED, THE SYSTEM WILL PROMPT THE USER TO           01880020
             ENTER A QUESTION MARK OR A NULL LINE AFTER A COMMAND THAT  01890020
             HAS ISSUED A MESSAGE WITH MULTIPLE LEVELS OF OUTPUT.       01892020
))NOPAUSE  - SPECIFIES THAT SECOND LEVEL MESSAGES WILL NOT BE AVAILABLE 01900020
             TO THE USER WHILE OPERATING IN A COMMAND PROCEDURE.        01950020
))MSGID    - SPECIFIES THAT TERMINAL MESSAGES WILL INCLUDE MESSAGE      02000020
             IDENTIFIERS.                                               02050020
))NOMSGID  - SPECIFIES THAT TERMINAL MESSAGES WILL NOT INCLUDE          02100020
             MESSAGE IDENTIFIERS.                                       02150020
))MODE     - SPECIFIES THAT THE USER WISHES TO RECEIVE MODE MESSAGES    02200002
             AT HIS TERMINAL                                            05200002
))NOMODE   - SPECIFIES THAT THE USER DOES NOT WISH TO RECEIVE           08200002
             MODE MESSAGES AT HIS TERMINAL                              11200002
))PREFIX('PREFIX')                                                      14200002
           - SPECIFIES A PREFIX WHICH WILL BE APPENDED TO ALL           17200002
             NON-FULLY QUALIFIED DSNAMES.                               20200002
    'PREFIX'                                                            23200002
           - IS ANY VALID DSNAME QUALIFIER OF 1-7 ALPHAMERIC            26200002
             CHARACTERS THAT BEGINS WITH AN ALPHABETIC OR               29200002
             NATIONAL CHARACTER                                         32200002
))NOPREFIX - SPECIFIES NO PREFIXING OF DSNAMES BY ANY QUALIFIER         35200002
             WILL BE PERFORMED                                          38200002
))WTPMSG   - SPECIFIES THE USER WISHES TO RECEIVE WRITE TO              41200002
             PROGRAMMER MESSAGES AT HIS TERMINAL                        44200002
))NOWTPMSG - SPECIFIES THE USER DOES NOT WISH TO RECEIVE WRITE TO       47200002
             PROGRAMMER MESSAGES AT HIS TERMINAL                        50200002
))LIST     - SPECIFIES THAT THE USER PROFILE IS TO BE LISTED.           53200002
